  "names": [],
  "id": "482181609",
  "subject": [],
  "title": "Mineral Water Hospital site",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/architecturalcomplex"
  ],
  "details": "<p>La Trobe-Bateman and Niblett note that there was clearly at least one high-status building on this site. In the east wing the\u00a0remains of two heated rooms, part of a corridor containing a geometric mosaic, part of a large room containing a geometric mosaic comprising intersecting circles were discovered. In the west wing, another mosaic that likely pertains to a second structure was found. It is possible that\u00a0a dedication to Sulis by Tiberius Claudius Sollemnis came from this site.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Remains of a large building discovered in Aquae Sulis. The site now lies on the grounds of the Royal National Hospital for Rheumatic Diseases.",
